{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-default-page-js","path":"/tutorials/bios_t1","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<h2 id=\"alane-suhr\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#alane-suhr\" aria-label=\"alane suhr permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Alane Suhr</h2>\n<p>PhD Student, Cornell University<br>\n<a href=\"mailto:suhr@cs.cornell.edu\">suhr@cs.cornell.edu</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://alanesuhr.com\">https://alanesuhr.com</a><br>\nAlane's research focuses on grounded natural language\nunderstanding. Alane has designed crowdsourcing\ntasks for collecting language data to study\nsituated natural language understanding. Alane\nco-presented a tutorial in ACL 2018.</p>\n<h2 id=\"clara-vania\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#clara-vania\" aria-label=\"clara vania permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Clara Vania</h2>\n<p>Applied Scientist, Amazon<br>\n<a href=\"mailto:vaniclar@amazon.co.uk\">vaniclar@amazon.co.uk</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://claravania.github.io/\">https://claravania.github.io/</a><br>\nHer research focuses on crowdsourcing, transfer\nlearning, and multilingual NLU. Recently, she has\nbeen working on semi-automatic data collection\nfor natural language inference and crowdsourcing\nmethods for question answering.</p>\n<h2 id=\"nikita-nangia\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#nikita-nangia\" aria-label=\"nikita nangia permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Nikita Nangia</h2>\n<p>PhD student, New York University<br>\n<a href=\"mailto:nikitanangia@nyu.edu\">nikitanangia@nyu.edu</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://woollysocks.github.io\">https://woollysocks.github.io</a><br>\nNikita’s work focuses on crowdsourcing methods and data creation for natural language understandingsoft. Her recent work explores using incentive structures to illicit creative examples. Nikita coorganized a tutorial on latent structure models for NLP at ACL 2019.</p>\n<h2 id=\"maarten-sap\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#maarten-sap\" aria-label=\"maarten sap permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Maarten Sap</h2>\n<p>PhD student, University of Washington<br>\n<a href=\"mailto:msap@cs.washington.edu\">msap@cs.washington.edu</a>\n<a href=\"http://maartensap.com/\">http://maartensap.com/</a><br>\nHis research focuses on endowing NLP systems\nwith social intelligence and social commonsense,\nand understanding social inequality and bias in\nlanguage. His substantial experience with crowdsourcing\nincludes the collecting of the SOCIALIQA\ncommonsense benchmark as well as the creation\nof knowledge graphs with inferential knowledge\n(ATOMIC, Social Bias Frames).</p>\n<h2 id=\"mark-yatskar\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#mark-yatskar\" aria-label=\"mark yatskar permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Mark Yatskar</h2>\n<p>Assistant Professor, University of Pennsylvania<br>\n<a href=\"mailto:myatskar@seas.upenn.edu\">myatskar@seas.upenn.edu</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://markyatskar.com/\">https://markyatskar.com/</a><br>\nHis research focuses on the intersection of natural\nlanguage processing and computer vision. Mark’s\nwork has resulted in the creation of datasets such as\nimSitu, QuAC and WinoBias and recent research\nhas focused on gender bias in visual recognition\nand coreference resolution.</p>\n<h2 id=\"sam-bowman\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#sam-bowman\" aria-label=\"sam bowman permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Sam Bowman</h2>\n<p>Assistant Professor, New York University<br>\n<a href=\"mailto:bowman@nyu.edu\">bowman@nyu.edu</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://cims.nyu.edu/~sbowman/\">https://cims.nyu.edu/~sbowman/</a><br>\nSam works on data creation, benchmarking, and\nmodel analysis for NLU and computational linguistics.\nSam has had a substantial role in several NLU\ndatasets, including SNLI, MNLI, XNLI, CoLA,\nand BLiMP, and his recent work has focused on experimentally\nevaluating methods for crowdsourced\ncorpus construction.</p>\n<h2 id=\"yoav-artzi\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#yoav-artzi\" aria-label=\"yoav artzi permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Yoav Artzi</h2>\n<p>Associate Professor, Cornell University<br>\n<a href=\"mailto:yoav@cs.cornell.edu\">yoav@cs.cornell.edu</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://yoavartzi.com/\">https://yoavartzi.com/</a><br>\nYoav's research focuses on learning expressive\nmodels for natural language understanding, most\nrecently in situated interactive scenarios. Yoav\nled tutorials on semantic parsing in ACL 2013,\nEMNLP 2014 and AAAI 2015.</p>","frontmatter":{"title":"Bios of Tutorial 1 Presenters","seo":{"browserTitle":"Bios T1 | EMNLP 2021","title":"Bios of Tutorial 1 Presenters | EMNLP 2021","description":"Bios of the tutorial presents of T1: Crowdsourcing Beyond Annotation: Case Studies in Benchmark Data Collection"}}},"footerData":{"edges":[{"node":{"id":"9b1aa201-3a7f-5cc9-997e-57fc28936f81","frontmatter":{"logoImage":{"image":"/img/acl-logo.png","imageAlt":"Association for Computational Linguistics","taglines":["EMNLP 2021","7th – 11th November | Online and in the Dominican Republic"],"orgLink":"https://www.aclweb.org"}}}}]},"navbarData":{"edges":[{"node":{"id":"d7b2310f-0eb2-592b-ae9b-16ed0c9c01e9","frontmatter":{"logoImage":null,"menuItems":[{"label":"registration","linkType":null,"linkURL":"/registration","longLabel":null,"otherPatterns":null},{"label":"blog","linkType":null,"linkURL":"/blog","longLabel":null,"otherPatterns":null},{"label":"calls","linkType":null,"linkURL":"/call-for-papers","longLabel":null,"otherPatterns":null},{"label":"program","linkType":"internal","linkURL":"/program","longLabel":null,"otherPatterns":["/program","/tutorials","/workshops","/keynotes"]},{"label":"organizers","linkType":null,"linkURL":"/organizers","longLabel":null,"otherPatterns":null},{"label":"sponsors","linkType":null,"linkURL":"/sponsors","longLabel":null,"otherPatterns":null},{"label":"venue","linkType":null,"linkURL":"/venue","longLabel":"Venue and Accomodations","otherPatterns":null},{"label":"home","linkType":null,"linkURL":"/","longLabel":"Landing Page","otherPatterns":null}]}}},{"node":{"id":"eee84e31-e133-51f1-8698-670ecf311084","frontmatter":{"logoImage":null,"menuItems":[{"label":"program","linkType":null,"linkURL":"/program","longLabel":null,"otherPatterns":null},{"label":"workshops","linkType":"internal","linkURL":"/workshops","longLabel":null,"otherPatterns":null},{"label":"tutorials","linkType":"internal","linkURL":"/tutorials","longLabel":null,"otherPatterns":null},{"label":"keynotes","linkType":"internal","linkURL":"/keynotes"